    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0292" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Stockton</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 30, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: An instruction, numbered 2, and dated the
                    29th instant, has been addressed to your successor, Mr. King, of which, as it
                    relates to a subject of present moment, I have deemed it expedient to send you a
                    transcript, which you will find enclosed. It is thought desirable that the views
                    therein expressed should be communicated to the Papal government without
                    delay.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John P. Stockton</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Rome</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
